# Real TLS certificates and keys live in this directory as fullchain.pem and
# privkey.pem -- copy or symlink your real files here (e.g. from certbot /
# Let's Encrypt). Those exact names are git-ignored (rule below) so your real
# certs are never accidentally staged, and so a symlinked deploy doesn't show
# up as a "modified"/"typechange" on every `git pull`.
#
# The tracked *.pem.example files are placeholders that keep this directory and
# its setup instructions visible in a fresh clone. To bring up the stack:
#   cp fullchain.pem.example fullchain.pem   # then replace with your real cert chain
#   cp privkey.pem.example   privkey.pem     # then replace with your real private key
# (or symlink the real files to those names). docker-compose mounts
# ./ssl/fullchain.pem and ./ssl/privkey.pem into the nginx container.
#
# DO NOT commit real certificates or private keys.
*.pem
